<Site title="About · Species bingo" description="Who made Species bingo, why, and how to suggest a new list." heading="About" path="/about/">
  <div class="site__body prose">
    <h2>Who made it</h2>
    <p>Species bingo is made by Wild &amp; Native Gardens, a small project about wildlife, native plants and getting outside to look at them.</p>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>Spotting things is better with friends. Bingo gives a walk, a boat ride or a garden visit a little game on top: you look harder, you point things out, and whoever you are with holds the other card.</p>

    <h2>Free, and nothing to sign up for</h2>
    <p>There are no accounts, no ads and no tracking. It is free. See <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for the short version of what is stored on your phone.</p>

    <h2>Suggest a list</h2>
    <p>Each game is one list of things to spot, with a photo and a short ID tip for each. If you would like a list for your own trip, park or garden, get in touch with Wild &amp; Native Gardens and say where it is and what you hope to find.</p>
  </div>
</Site>
